\", \\"filename\\": \\"koto_Goalbz Tag.wav\\", \\"status\\": \\"pending\\", \\"track_id\\": 17, \\"track_name\\": \\"Goalbz Tag\\", \\"fl_state_hash\\": \\"8289dbe075ed706d\\", \\"rendered_at\\": null, \\"analysis\\": null}, {\\"kind\\": \\"stem\\", \\"filename\\": \\"koto_Insert 18.wav\\", \\"status\\": \\"pending\\", \\"track_id\\": 18, \\"track_name\\": \\"Insert 18\\", \\"fl_state_hash\\": \\"05f7237e8be05c2a\\", \\"rendered_at\\": null, \\"analysis\\": null}, {\\"kind\\": \\"stem\\", \\"filename\\": \\"koto_Insert 19.wav\\", \\"status\\": \\"pending\\", \\"track_id\\": 19, \\"track_name\\": \\"Insert 19\\", \\"fl_state_hash\\": \\"9c531ff11020c93b\\", \\"rendered_at\\": null, \\"analysis\\": null}, {\\"kind\\": \\"stem\\", \\"filename\\": \\"koto_Insert 20.wav\\", \\"status\\": \\"pending\\", \\"track_id\\": 20, \\"track_name\\": \\"Insert 20\\", \\"fl_state_hash\\": \\"d80d8667a3e00814\\", \\"rendered_at\\": null, \\"analysis\\": null}], \\"masters\\": [], \\"references\\": [], \\"drops\\": []}"}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": ["ToolUseBlock(id=\'toolu_01EfrVMYMoiXPSBx5XkpzLns\', caller=DirectCaller(type=\'direct\'), input={}, name=\'read_project_history\', type=\'tool_use\')"]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01EfrVMYMoiXPSBx5XkpzLns", "content": "{\\"ok\\": true, \\"project_name\\": \\"koto\\", \\"history_markdown\\": \\"# koto \\\\u2014 StudioMind history\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-04-23 20:46 UTC\\\\n**First session \\\\u2014 initial batch render & analysis (koto)**\\\\n\\\\n- All 20 mixer tracks + master rendered for the first time.\\\\n- Tracks 1 (Omnisphere), 11 (Kontakt 5), 12 (Kontakt 5 #2), 13 (Omnisphere #2): **SILENT** \\\\u2014 likely unused/muted or no pattern assigned yet.\\\\n- Tracks 18\\\\u201320 (Insert 18/19/20): failed to read \\\\u2014 likely empty inserts, nothing routed in.\\\\n- Master: -14.2 LUFS, 0.0 dBTP (true peak is clipping). Loud and hot.\\\\n\\\\n**Active stems summary:**\\\\n| Track | Name | LUFS | True Peak | Centroid | Notes |\\\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\\\n| 2 | [reese] bob cochonou | -27.3 | -18.1 dB | 156 Hz | Very sub/low heavy |\\\\n| 3 | [808] choucroute | -16.6 | -5.6 dB | 206 Hz | Loud, full-range 808, lots of low-mid/mid |\\\\n| 4 | JP - Simmie Hat | -34.9 | -15.2 dB | 10.2 kHz | Air-heavy, fine |\\\\n| 5 | JP - Low Hat | -37.6 | -22.1 dB | 3.7 kHz | Quiet, OK |\\\\n| 6 | JP - Crack Hat | -30.5 | -14.5 dB | 5.6 kHz | Fine |\\\\n| 7 | JP - Greek Clap | -28.5 | -10.9 dB | 4.0 kHz | Good body+air balance |\\\\n| 8 | JP - Metal Clap | -25.9 | -10.4 dB | 5.2 kHz | Decent, slight low-mid weight |\\\\n| 9 | JP - Bongo Perc | -22.8 | -4.5 dB | 1.5 kHz | Hot true peak; very low-mid/mid heavy |\\\\n| 10 | Nuclear Kick | -11.0 | -4.0 dB | 371 Hz | Extremely loud; dominant sub/low |\\\\n| 14 | koto thing | -24.1 | -8.6 dB | 2.2 kHz | Low-mid/mid heavy; potential mud with 808 |\\\\n| 15 | koto thing #2 | -36.3 | -23.0 dB | 3.8 kHz | Quiet, OK |\\\\n| 16 | Cymatics Reverse Air | -29.3 | -13.3 dB | 4.1 kHz | Low-mid spike (71.6) vs. clean sub |\\\\n| 17 | Goalbz Tag | -23.3 | -11.3 dB | 2.4 kHz | Mid-focused, no sub (intentional tag) |\\\\n\\\\n**Key issues identified:**\\\\n1. **Master true peak = 0.0 dBTP** \\\\u2014 clipping/limiting at ceiling. No headroom.\\\\n2. **Nuclear Kick (10)** at -11 LUFS is far too loud relative to the mix \\\\u2014 dominant driver of clipping.\\\\n3. **808 (3)** at -16.6 LUFS is very hot and full-range (sub through air), likely fighting the kick in the sub/low bands.\\\\n4. **Kick + 808 + Reese + Bongo all stacking sub/low** \\\\u2014 major low-end congestion expected.\\\\n5. **koto thing (14)** has high low-mid energy (100.6) \\\\u2014 could be muddying the melodic space.\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-04-23 21:00 UTC\\\\n[Auto-saved on context compaction]\\\\n\\\\n# Session Summary: koto (First Render & Analysis)\\\\n\\\\n## Project State\\\\n**Project:** koto | **Status:** First session \\\\u2014 all 20 tracks + master rendered for the first time\\\\n\\\\n### Render Results\\\\n- **18 of 20 stems rendered successfully** (44.1 kHz, stereo, ~182.5 s duration)\\\\n- **Master rendered:** koto_Master.wav\\\\n- **4 failures:** Tracks 18\\\\u201320 (Insert 18/19/20) \\\\u2014 system errors; likely empty/unused inserts\\\\n\\\\n### Silent/Unused Tracks (LUFS: -120.0, True Peak: -200.0 dB)\\\\nTracks 1, 11, 12, 13 are confirmed silent \\\\u2014 no content or muted instruments:\\\\n- Track 1: Omnisphere [64bit]\\\\n- Track 11: Kontakt 5\\\\n- Track 12: Kontakt 5 #2\\\\n- Track 13: Omnisphere [64bit] #2\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Active Stems \\\\u2014 Key Measurements\\\\n\\\\n| Track | Name | LUFS | True Peak | Spectral Centroid | Status |\\\\n|-------|------|------|-----------|-------------------|--------|\\\\n| 2 | [reese] bob cochonou | -27.3 | -18.1 dB | 157 Hz | Sub/low heavy |\\\\n| 3 | [808] choucroute | -16.6 | -5.6 dB | 206 Hz | Full-range, hot |\\\\n| 4 | JP - Simmie Hat | -34.9 | -15.2 dB | 10.2 kHz | Air-dominant |\\\\n| 10 | Nuclear Kick | **-11.0** | **-4.0 dB** | 371 Hz | **Extremely loud** |\\\\n| 14 | koto thing | -24.1 | -8.6 dB | 2.2 kHz | Low-mid heavy |\\\\n| 9 | JP - Bongo Perc | -22.8 | -4.5 dB | 1.5 kHz | Hot; mid-focused |\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Master Analysis\\\\n- **LUFS:** -14.2 dB\\\\n- **True Peak:** **0.0 dBTP** \\\\u26a0\\\\ufe0f **Clipping at ceiling; no headroom**\\\\n- **Spectral Centroid:** 1997.8 Hz\\\\n- **Sub balance (0\\\\u2013200 Hz):**\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-04-23 21:08 UTC\\\\n[Auto-saved on disconnect \\\\u2014 last agent response:]\\\\n\\\\nI don\'t see a dedicated \\\\\\"piano\\\\\\" track in the project \\\\u2014 no track is explicitly labelled piano. Looking at the channel rack, **track 14 \\\\\\"koto thing\\\\\\"** is the most melodic/harmonic instrument that could reasonably be called a piano (Kontakt 5 tracks are silent, Omnisphere tracks are silent). I\'ll proceed on track 14 as you\'ve confirmed.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n**Before values (from the initial render):**\\\\n- low_mid: **100.6**\\\\n- LUFS: **-24.1**\\\\n- True peak: **-8.6 dB**\\\\n\\\\n**Predicted low_mid delta:**\\\\nA -2 dB bell at 300 Hz with Q=1.5 covers roughly the 200\\\\u2013450 Hz range. The analysis \\\\\\"low_mid\\\\\\" band spans 250\\\\u2013500 Hz, so 300 Hz sits squarely in it. I expect the low_mid reading to drop by approximately **1.5\\\\u20132.0 dB** (slightly less than the full cut because the band energy is averaged across the full 250\\\\u2013500 Hz range, not just 300 Hz). The low band (60\\\\u2013250 Hz) may dip very slightly (~0.3 dB) at its top edge.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\nNow: snapshot \\\\u2192 apply \\\\u2192 re-render.\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-04-23 21:24 UTC\\\\n- Deepened built-in EQ band 1 on track 14 \\\\\\"koto thing\\\\\\": 308 Hz from -1.98 dB \\\\u2192 -4.0 dB (added -2 dB, Q\\\\u22480.55/bandwidth). Track 14 low_mid: 99.9 \\\\u2192 99.3 (\\\\u22120.6). Master low_mid: 99.9 \\\\u2192 99.2 (\\\\u22120.7). Master LUFS: -24.4 \\\\u2192 -24.6. Change kept.\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-04-23 21:34 UTC\\\\n- Track 14 \\\\\\"koto thing\\\\\\" built-in EQ band 1: -3.0 dB @ 287 Hz, bandwidth\\\\u22480.35 (Q\\\\u22481.5). Previous state was -4.0 dB @ 308 Hz. Stem low_mid: 99.3 \\\\u2192 98.5 (-0.8 dB). Master LUFS: -24.6 \\\\u2192 -24.9. True peak: -9.4 \\\\u2192 -10.1 dB. Note: built-in EQ coarse resolution landed -3 dB/287 Hz instead of requested -2 dB/300 Hz \\\\u2014 recommend Pro-Q 3 for precision on this track.\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-04-23 21:39 UTC\\\\n[Auto-saved on disconnect \\\\u2014 last agent response:]\\\\n\\\\n**Summary:** The -3 dB cut at 287 Hz on \\\\\\"koto thing\\\\\\" trimmed **-0.8 dB low_mid** and **-1.8 dB low** on the stem \\\\u2014 slightly asymmetric because 287 Hz sits right on the low/low_mid boundary. Master moved from **-24.6 \\\\u2192 -24.9 LUFS** and true peak dropped **0.7 dB**, giving a little more headroom.\\\\n\\\\n**One caveat to flag:** The built-in EQ\'s normalized gain scale resolved to **-3.0 dB @ 287 Hz** rather 